// "Fight(a, b)" ([CR#701.14a]) — the bare-verb pattern TWIN: "whenever `a`
// fights `b`". Both combatants are patients: `a` rides the master form's `who`
// slot and `b` its `on` slot, and the engine binds them to the fact's two
// patient coordinates (`object`/`patient`) — Fight has no performer. Expands to
// the `Act` master form.
(
    name: "Fight",
    template: "${0} fights ${1}",
    kinds: [EventFilter],
    params: [Predicate, Predicate],
    body: Act(verb: Fight, who: Param(0), on: Param(1)),
)
